{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From.</b> The ends of the earth, for they were in Babylon, and it is far from their land." "<b>And from its nobles.</b> Its great ones, for they are drawn from everything, like ואצלתי מן הרוח (Numbers 11:17), and similarly ואל אצילי בני ישראל (Exodus 24:11). Or its meaning is: from among its nobles."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:20.093080283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}